// The Hash/Hasher shape as a running program: a multi-module `rene build`
// with the trait pair and a byte-splitting bounded generic at the package
// root, Bernstein's djb2 in its own module, the hashable types (a ground
// impl and a generic `Pair` whose impl recurses through both bounds) in
// another, and the bounded API in a third — every bound spelled through a
// qualified `super::` path. The printed values are the real djb2 digests
// of the little-endian byte streams, pinned against an independent
// reference computation.

// RUN: %rene build --manifest-path %S/trait_hash/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir %rrc_linker | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LISTING

// LISTING: {{[/\\]}}dev{{[/\\]}}hashdemo

// RUN: %t.bdir/dev/hashdemo%exe_ext | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OUT

// djb2 over LE(1) ++ LE(2)…
// OUT: 7944528385982877352
// …over LE(3) ++ LE(4)…
// OUT-NEXT: 445791163684897836
// …and Pair{Point(3,4), Point(5,6)} folds the same state onward.
// OUT-NEXT: 5582476884098275031
